<summary>curl example and sample response</summary>

```bash
curl -s http://localhost:3000/network-status | jq
```

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "network": "testnet",
    "horizonUrl": "https://horizon-testnet.stellar.org",
    "latestLedger": {
      "sequence": 1284901,
      "closedAt": "2024-07-01T12:00:05.000Z",
      "transactionCount": 4,
      "operationCount": 6
    },
    "fees": {
      "baseFeeInStroops": 100,
      "baseFeeInXLM": "0.0000100"
    },
    "protocol": {
      "version": 21
    }
  }
}
```

</details>

### `GET /network/base-fee`

Returns the current network base fee in both stroops and XLM, the latest ledger sequence, and a boolean `isSurge` flag that signals whether the network is currently experiencing elevated fees.

This endpoint is useful for wallets and transaction builders that need a quick, authoritative answer to "what is the minimum fee right now?"

<details>
<summary>curl example and sample response</summary>

```bash
curl -s http://localhost:3000/network/base-fee | jq
```

